.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 7, 2026
.Dt PKG-BINARY 5
.Os "pkg-mgr 0.1.0 experimental"
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg-binary
.Nd local binary package directory transport
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A local-binary-directory-v2 bundle transports one registered host package into
another initialized private root.
It is a directory of ordinary files, not an archive or a production store format.
It provides byte-identity checks, not remote publisher authentication.
The caller supplies the absolute bundle path, descriptor SHA-256 pin and expected
compiler target.
.Pp
The bundle and destination must remain under caller control with a single writer.
Imported executable content and build recipes remain trusted by the caller.
No native Aether ABI, service activation, installation to a live prefix or
power-loss durability is implied.
.Sh DIRECTORY LAYOUT
The bundle has exactly these top-level entries:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa artifact.kv
Canonical descriptor binding the other metadata tables.
.It Pa package.tsv
Exact permission-tracked pkg-state-v2 record, including embedded evidence,
dependencies, file hashes, sizes, paths and modes.
.It Pa target.kv
Canonical host identity record.
.It Pa modes.tsv
One ordinary mode, tab, logical path per file, in package-record order.
.It Pa dependencies.tsv
One dependency name, tab, exact registered-record SHA-256 per dependency,
in package-record order.
An empty dependency list has an empty table.
.It Pa files/
Regular-file blobs named by their 64-character lowercase SHA-256.
Repeated content shares one blob within this bundle.
Unreferenced blobs are rejected.
.El
.Pp
Links, hard-linked files and special entries are rejected before content is consumed.
Unknown top-level entries are rejected.
All five metadata tables must be readable regular files.
.Sh ARTIFACT DESCRIPTOR
The descriptor has these key=value lines in exact order, each ending in newline.
There are no comments, blank lines, duplicate keys or optional keys.
The four digest values are 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li format
Must be local-binary-directory-v2.
.It Li record_sha256
Hash of package.tsv.
.It Li target_sha256
Hash of target.kv.
.It Li modes_sha256
Hash of modes.tsv.
.It Li dependencies_sha256
Hash of dependencies.tsv.
.It Li authenticity
Must be not-proven.
.It Li service_activation
Must be unsupported.
.El
.Pp
The caller's descriptor pin binds artifact.kv itself.
A locally calculated pin demonstrates integrity for one's own build.
A pin delivered beside an untrusted download does not authenticate that download.
.Sh TARGET RECORD
The target record has these key=value lines in exact order:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li format
Must be host-binary-target-v1.
.It Li host_os
Must match the running host's uname -s output.
.It Li host_arch
Must match the running host's uname -m output.
.It Li compiler_target
Must match the caller's explicit expected target.
.It Li modes
Must be recorded-0000-0777.
.El
.Pp
These comparisons do not prove minimum OS version, CPU features, ABI compatibility
or native Aether support.
The package must contain a manifest-bound host observation at
.Pa usr/local/share/pkg-mgr/NAME/host.kv .
Its target runtime must be host-only.
Other prefixes and runtimes require an explicit extension.
Metadata observations do not grant authority.
.Sh FILE AND DEPENDENCY TABLES
Modes are exactly four octal digits from 0000 through 0777 and must equal the
package record's modes, in the same file order.
Set-ID and sticky bits are rejected.
File sizes, content hashes and paths are checked through candidate state validation.
The directory does not preserve ownership, timestamps, ACLs, extended attributes,
directory modes or empty directories.
.Pp
Dependency fingerprints must match already registered records and the package's
bound host observations.
Import dependencies explicitly before dependents; no resolver or version substitution
is implemented.
Neither import nor export edits world.
.Sh VALIDATION AND PUBLICATION
Export first verifies registered state and refuses an occupied binaries/NAME.
Import verifies existing state, descriptor binding, schema, host identity, modes,
dependency fingerprints and blob content, then constructs a private candidate.
Existing state validation checks candidate sizes, evidence and ownership conflicts.
The stage and record are published in separate renames.
.Pp
An ordinary failure between publication renames cleans only this invocation's
newly published, unregistered stage.
A crash can leave an occupied unregistered stage; import refuses to overwrite it.
Recover can publish the missing record only after validating the existing stage
against the exact pinned bundle.
It does not repair mismatched content.
There is no automatic recovery, package deletion or crash-atomic transaction.
.Sh COMPATIBILITY
V2 transport requires permission-tracked pkg-state-v2 records.
Earlier local-binary-directory-v1 bundles are rejected.
Rebuild and register into a fresh private root; no automatic migration rewrites
historical records, bundles or evidence.
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the checkout, with a host C compiler, Python 3, GNU Make, sh and a SHA-256 tool,
run the real bytecount lifecycle fixture:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sh tests/bytecount-integration.sh
.Ed
.Pp
It rejects corrupted source, builds and registers the command, exports a local
bundle, imports it into a fresh private root and checks imported execution.
A PASS line and retained_root identify successful evidence and the private output.
It does not download sources or write to a live prefix.
The compiler target is a host observation for this experiment, not a compatibility
policy for arbitrary downloaded software.
.Pp
For a previously exported bundle, inspect the descriptor as data:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat "$bundle/artifact.kv"
.Ed
.Pp
Here bundle is the absolute path to binaries/bytecount beneath the retained root.
Never source a metadata file as shell code.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ROOT/binaries/NAME
Exported local bundle.
.It Pa ROOT/stage/NAME
Imported staged payload.
.It Pa ROOT/state/packages/NAME.tsv
Imported package record.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg-mgr 1 ,
.Xr pkg-state 5
.Pp
See docs/BINARY-PACKAGE.md for workflow and validation context and
docs/IMPORT-RECOVERY.md for exact pinned recovery.
